# R47 Track B — PER-ARM POSITIVE CONTROL for the register-at-birth conversion.
#
# CELL: arm = `Callable[T]` PARAMETER (`calls.rs`, `__callable_N`) ·
# disposition = TRANSFERRED ONWARD into a container that outlives the call,
# read back afterwards · payload = String.
#
# The argument is a NAMED FUNCTION, not a closure literal, so the fixture
# isolates the call-result producer from the separate (and still-open)
# `__gorget_closure_env_alloc` leak — see
# `indirect_callable_param_call_result_leak.gg`.
#
# ⚠ THE SECOND-LIVE-SLOT REQUIREMENT — both runtime release paths self-null by
# design; only a value copied onward can observe an extra drop.
#
# ⚠ GREEN AT HEAD AND AFTER, AND I COULD NOT MAKE IT RED — WHICH IS THE
# FINDING, NOT AN EXCUSE. Two deliberate breaks were built and run against
# this shape: (1) `call_indirect_tracked` made to register the result TWICE,
# and (2) the enum/struct ownership transfer (`emit_enum_init_owned`'s
# post-init unregister) disabled. Both left this program CLEAN 3/3. The reason
# is the mechanism this whole net is built around: at THIS consuming position
# the transfer either zeroes the source slot (`move_zero`, the collection and
# bare-assign paths) or removes its registration, and a second `drop_if_alive`
# through the SAME slot is a no-op because `gorget_string_free` self-nulls by
# design. So an over-registration is not merely unobserved here, it is
# structurally absorbed — and this fixture pins that the conversion did not
# disturb the consuming position's value behaviour or introduce corruption.
# The direction that CAN be observed is pinned by the three
# `combinator_*_transferred_no_double_free.gg` controls, where the adapter's
# Move-assign leaves the pointer in a SECOND LIVE SLOT: those go RED (ASan
# `attempting double-free`, 3/3) against the conversion without its
# compensating transfer.
#
# INSTRUMENT: `security_safe_no_leak`, C lane only.
from std.collections import Vector

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

String maker():
    return mk("hel", "lo")

void collect(Callable[String()] f):
    Vector[String] v = Vector[String]()
    v.push(f())
    v.push(f())
    print(v.len())
    print(v[0])
    print(v[1])

void main():
    collect(maker)
